  "question": {
    "text": "The point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math> lies on the hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> having eccentricity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If the tangent and normal at $P$ to the hyperbola intersect its conjugate axis at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> respectively, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is equal to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math> lies on hyperbola.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>24</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Given, eccentricity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>On solving equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, we get<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math><br />Hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><msub><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Equation of tangent is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math><br />at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math><br />Equation&nbsp;of normal is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math><br />at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Apply distance formula,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
